    "asOf": "2026-10-14",
    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Michelle Rodriguez is a Democrat representing the 53rd District in the California State Assembly. She was elected in 2024 and previously served on the California Commission on Peace Officer Standards and Training. She authored AB 1628, a passed bill regarding child protection and safe surrender. Her other passed bills include AB 2006 to create daycare centers in state office buildings, AB 2453 on off-highway vehicles, and AB 744 on tied-house restrictions for alcohol sales. She co-authored Leno's Law (SB 712), which expands smog check exemptions for collector vehicles, and supports manufacturing and regulatory reform. She also introduced AB 2628 to amend the County Fire Service Retirement Law.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5],
